==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|framoþjo-|lang=ang}} from {{proto|Germanic|fram-|lang=ang}} (related to ‘[[from]]’).  Cognates include Old Saxon {{term|fremithi|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|vreemd|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|framadi|lang=goh}}, and Gothic {{term|𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌼𐌰𐌸𐍃|lang=got|sc=Goth}}.

